{"type":"message","id":"bae93e8a","parentId":"b4421896","timestamp":"2026-02-10T17:50:43.465Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to start a fresh session using the NVIDIA Kimi K2.5 model and confirm that the model is active.\n\nAs a subagent, I need to:\n1. Understand my role - I'm a subagent spawned to handle a specific task\n2. Complete the task - \"Start a fresh session using the NVIDIA Kimi K2.5 model. Confirm that the model is active.\"\n3. Stay focused and complete the task\n4. Return a concise report\n\nI need to check what tools I have available. Looking at my toolset, I don't see any direct way to start a new session or switch models. The subagent context says I was created to handle this task, but it doesn't provide the mechanism to actually do it.\n\nIn OpenClaw, models are typically managed through the system itself. I should check if there are any commands or ways to verify the current model. However, as a subagent, my capabilities might be limited.\n\nLet me think about this:\n- The user is asking me to \"start a fresh session using the NVIDIA Kimi K2.5 model\"\n- This likely means they want me to ensure that a session is running with that model\n- \"Confirm that the model is active\" means I need to verify it's working\n\nBut as a subagent, I'm already in a session. The model that's running this subagent might be something else. Perhaps the main agent wants me to spawn a new subagent with the specific model? But that doesn't seem right because subagents inherit the main agent's model.\n\nMaybe the task is simpler: Just confirm what model is currently active, and if it's not Kimi K2.5, note that? Or maybe I need to check system status?\n\nLet me read the available tools again. I can:\n- read, write, edit files\n- exec shell commands\n- process (manage background sessions)\n- web_search, web_fetch\n- browser, canvas\n- nodes\n- message\n- tts\n\nI don't have a direct tool to control the model selection. However, I could potentially:\n1. Check the current session status somehow\n2. Run a command to see model information\n3. Look at configuration files\n\nThe OpenClaw CLI might have commands to check or set the model. The AGENTS.md mentions: \"If unsure, ask the user to run `openclaw help` (or `openclaw gateway --help`) and paste the output.\"\n\nBut as a subagent, I'm supposed to just do the task, not ask the user. However, I could potentially use `exec` to run `openclaw` commands.\n\nLet me try to check the system status using `openclaw` commands. I could run something like `openclaw gateway status` or `openclaw --help` to see available options.\n\nActually, the AGENTS.md says: \"To manage the Gateway daemon service (start/stop/restart): - openclaw gateway status - openclaw gateway start - openclaw gateway stop - openclaw gateway restart\"\n\nBut that's about the gateway service, not the model. There might be other commands for model selection.\n\nI could also check the environment or configuration files in the workspace. The model configuration might be stored somewhere.\n\nLet me try a few approaches:\n\n1. Check if there's a config file that defines the active model\n2. Use `openclaw` CLI to check model status\n3. Look at environment variables\n\nLet's start by exploring the workspace to see what's there.\n\nI should read files in the workspace directory: /root/.openclaw/workspace\n\nLet me see what files exist there.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you start a fresh session with the NVIDIA Kimi K2.5 model and confirm it's active. Let me check the current system status and available options."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-f4c8556f464446ba812b0eadf394ca22","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw --help"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":8251,"output":1677,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9928,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770745834434}}
{"type":"message","id":"8db5218c","parentId":"bae93e8a","timestamp":"2026-02-10T17:50:46.039Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-f4c8556f464446ba812b0eadf394ca22","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.9 (96c46ed) — IPC, but it's your phone.\n\nUsage: openclaw [options] [command]\n\nOptions:\n  --dev             Dev profile: isolate state under ~/.openclaw-dev, default\n                    gateway port 19001, and shift derived ports (browser/canvas)\n  -h, --help        display help for command\n  --no-color        Disable ANSI colors\n  --profile <name>  Use a named profile (isolates\n                    OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH under\n                    ~/.openclaw-<name>)\n  -V, --version     output the version number\n\nCommands:\n  acp               Agent Control Protocol tools\n  agent             Run an agent turn via the Gateway (use --local for embedded)\n  agents            Manage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n  approvals         Exec approvals\n  browser           Manage OpenClaw's dedicated browser (Chrome/Chromium)\n  channels          Channel management\n  completion        Generate shell completion script\n  config            Config helpers (get/set/unset). Run without subcommand for\n                    the wizard.\n  configure         Interactive prompt to set up credentials, devices, and agent\n                    defaults\n  cron              Cron scheduler\n  daemon            Gateway service (legacy alias)\n  dashboard         Open the Control UI with your current token\n  devices           Device pairing + token management\n  directory         Directory commands\n  dns               DNS helpers\n  docs              Docs helpers\n  doctor            Health checks + quick fixes for the gateway and channels\n  gateway           Gateway control\n  health            Fetch health from the running gateway\n  help              display help for command\n  hooks             Hooks tooling\n  logs              Gateway logs\n  memory            Memory search tools\n  message           Send messages and channel actions\n  models            Model configuration\n  node              Node control\n  nodes             Node commands\n  onboard           Interactive wizard to set up the gateway, workspace, and\n                    skills\n  pairing           Pairing helpers\n  plugins           Plugin management\n  reset             Reset local config/state (keeps the CLI installed)\n  sandbox           Sandbox tools\n  security          Security helpers\n  sessions          List stored conversation sessions\n  setup             Initialize ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json and the agent workspace\n  skills            Skills management\n  status            Show channel health and recent session recipients\n  system            System events, heartbeat, and presence\n  tui               Terminal UI\n  uninstall         Uninstall the gateway service + local data (CLI remains)\n  update            CLI update helpers\n  webhooks          Webhook helpers\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw channels login --verbose\n    Link personal WhatsApp Web and show QR + connection logs.\n  openclaw message send --target +15555550123 --message \"Hi\" --json\n    Send via your web session and print JSON result.\n  openclaw gateway --port 18789\n    Run the WebSocket Gateway locally.\n  openclaw --dev gateway\n    Run a dev Gateway (isolated state/config) on ws://127.0.0.1:19001.\n  openclaw gateway --force\n    Kill anything bound to the default gateway port, then start it.\n  openclaw gateway ...\n    Gateway control via WebSocket.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Run summary\" --deliver\n    Talk directly to the agent using the Gateway; optionally send the WhatsApp reply.\n  openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @mychat --message \"Hi\"\n    Send via your Telegram bot.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2571,"aggregated":"🦞 OpenClaw 2026.2.9 (96c46ed) — IPC, but it's your phone.\n\nUsage: openclaw [options] [command]\n\nOptions:\n  --dev             Dev profile: isolate state under ~/.openclaw-dev, default\n                    gateway port 19001, and shift derived ports (browser/canvas)\n  -h, --help        display help for command\n  --no-color        Disable ANSI colors\n  --profile <name>  Use a named profile (isolates\n                    OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR/OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH under\n                    ~/.openclaw-<name>)\n  -V, --version     output the version number\n\nCommands:\n  acp               Agent Control Protocol tools\n  agent             Run an agent turn via the Gateway (use --local for embedded)\n  agents            Manage isolated agents (workspaces + auth + routing)\n  approvals         Exec approvals\n  browser           Manage OpenClaw's dedicated browser (Chrome/Chromium)\n  channels          Channel management\n  completion        Generate shell completion script\n  config            Config helpers (get/set/unset). Run without subcommand for\n                    the wizard.\n  configure         Interactive prompt to set up credentials, devices, and agent\n                    defaults\n  cron              Cron scheduler\n  daemon            Gateway service (legacy alias)\n  dashboard         Open the Control UI with your current token\n  devices           Device pairing + token management\n  directory         Directory commands\n  dns               DNS helpers\n  docs              Docs helpers\n  doctor            Health checks + quick fixes for the gateway and channels\n  gateway           Gateway control\n  health            Fetch health from the running gateway\n  help              display help for command\n  hooks             Hooks tooling\n  logs              Gateway logs\n  memory            Memory search tools\n  message           Send messages and channel actions\n  models            Model configuration\n  node              Node control\n  nodes             Node commands\n  onboard           Interactive wizard to set up the gateway, workspace, and\n                    skills\n  pairing           Pairing helpers\n  plugins           Plugin management\n  reset             Reset local config/state (keeps the CLI installed)\n  sandbox           Sandbox tools\n  security          Security helpers\n  sessions          List stored conversation sessions\n  setup             Initialize ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json and the agent workspace\n  skills            Skills management\n  status            Show channel health and recent session recipients\n  system            System events, heartbeat, and presence\n  tui               Terminal UI\n  uninstall         Uninstall the gateway service + local data (CLI remains)\n  update            CLI update helpers\n  webhooks          Webhook helpers\n\nExamples:\n  openclaw channels login --verbose\n    Link personal WhatsApp Web and show QR + connection logs.\n  openclaw message send --target +15555550123 --message \"Hi\" --json\n    Send via your web session and print JSON result.\n  openclaw gateway --port 18789\n    Run the WebSocket Gateway locally.\n  openclaw --dev gateway\n    Run a dev Gateway (isolated state/config) on ws://127.0.0.1:19001.\n  openclaw gateway --force\n    Kill anything bound to the default gateway port, then start it.\n  openclaw gateway ...\n    Gateway control via WebSocket.\n  openclaw agent --to +15555550123 --message \"Run summary\" --deliver\n    Talk directly to the agent using the Gateway; optionally send the WhatsApp reply.\n  openclaw message send --channel telegram --target @mychat --message \"Hi\"\n    Send via your Telegram bot.\n\nDocs: https://docs.openclaw.ai/cli","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770745846037}}
